 36NE    9BE(48CA,X):NOT OBSERV:XUNDL-22022AH02,2019AH07                  202212
 36NE c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2022Ah02:                          
 36NE2c  Phys Rev Lett 129, 212502 (2022); and 2019Ah07:                        
 36NE3c  Phys Rev Lett 123, 212501 (2019).                                      
 36NE c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), Nov 30, 2022                          
 36NE c  Search for the observation of {+36}Ne nuclide proved negative, thus    
 36NE2c  suggesting that {+36}Ne is unbound towards neutron emission.           
 36NE c  2022Ah02 (also 2019Ah07): E({+48}Ca)=345 MeV/nucleon beam from RIBF    
 36NE2c  accelerator complex at RIKEN. Projectile fragments were separated and  
 36NE3c  identified in flight using the large-acceptance two-stage separator    
 36NE4c  BigRIPS spectrometer by tof-B|p-|DE method. The time-of-flight (tof)   
 36NE5c  was measured using two thin plastic scintillators placed at the        
 36NE6c  intermediate and final foci of the second stage of the BigRIPS         
 36NE7c  separator. Magnetic rigidity (B|p) was measured from position          
 36NE8c  measurement at the intermediate focus using the plastic scintillator.  
 36NE9c  The energy loss (|DE) was measured using an array of six silicon       
 36NEAc  detectors installed at the final focus. Optimum setting of B|p was     
 36NEBc  tuned to {+36}Ne, based on detailed simulations of the reaction and    
 36NECc  transmission with the LISE++ code. Measured atomic number (Z) versus   
 36NEDc  atomic mass/atomic number (A/Z) particle-identification plot.          
 36NEEc  Production target was irradiated with 5.25|*10{+17} {+48}Ca ions in    
 36NEFc  46.1 h. No events were observed for {+36}Ne, implying that this nuclide
 36NEGc  is unbound towards neutron emission. Estimated counts (2019Ah07) were  
 36NEHc  15.5 {I47} from EPAX 2.15 reaction model calculations, and 5.03 {I96}  
 36NEIc  from systematics of Q values using LISE++ simulations, with optimum    
 36NEJc  setting on total of {+33}F, and {+36}Ne+{+39}Na.                       
